    {
      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_24f40393",
      "@type": "OverallIntent",
      "instance_name": "overallintent_instance",
      "label": "the overallintent",
      "description": "meme-id: uglydolls_meme; hasOverallIntent: Harmful; overall-intent-description: The image features characters from the 'UglyDolls' franchise, which are intentionally designed to be visually unattractive. The overlaid text reads 'when you are that ugly you don't have a choice,' implying that being ugly is a permanent, defining, and perhaps burdensome condition. This message can be interpreted as harmful because it reinforces negative self-perception based on appearance, potentially contributing to body dysmorphia or low self-esteem in viewers who identify with the 'ugly' label. While the meme is not explicitly targeted at a specific protected group (like race, gender, or sexual orientation), it promotes a harmful societal message that equates ugliness with a lack of agency or choice, which can be psychologically damaging. The humor derives from the juxtaposition of the 'ugly' characters with the text suggesting they are forced into their appearance, but this framing can normalize and perpetuate the idea that physical appearance dictates one's worth or options, which is a form of aesthetic-based harm.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_29d83ed0"
      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
    },
