    {
      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_6db994ea",
      "@type": "BackgroundKnowledge",
      "instance_name": "aesthetic_based_harm_stereotype",
      "label": "Aesthetic-Based Harm Stereotype",
      "description": "The meme implicitly references the harmful societal stereotype that equates physical appearance with worth, agency, and self-esteem. It suggests that being 'ugly' is a permanent, defining condition that removes one's choice or control over their life, reinforcing negative self-perception and potentially contributing to body dysmorphia or low self-esteem. This stereotype is rooted in real-world cultural norms that prioritize conventional beauty standards and often marginalize those who do not conform.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_29d83ed0"
      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
    },
    {
      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_cc09c932",
      "@type": "BackgroundKnowledge",
      "instance_name": "uglydolls_franchise",
      "label": "UglyDolls Franchise",
      "description": "The meme relies on the real-world knowledge that 'UglyDolls' is a fictional franchise created by the studio DreamWorks Animation, which intentionally designs its characters to be visually unattractive as a form of subversion of traditional beauty standards. The franchise's premise is to celebrate 'ugliness' as a positive trait, which contrasts with the meme's text that frames ugliness as a negative, burdensome condition. Understanding this context is necessary to interpret the irony or contradiction in the meme.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_29d83ed0"
      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
    },
    {
      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_fd251695",
      "@type": "BackgroundKnowledge",
      "instance_name": "body_dysmorphia",
      "label": "Body Dysmorphia",
      "description": "The meme implicitly references the psychological condition of body dysmorphia, where individuals have a distorted perception of their own appearance, often fixating on perceived flaws. The text 'when you are that ugly you don't have a choice' can be interpreted as reinforcing the idea that one's appearance dictates their life, which may exacerbate feelings of inadequacy or self-hatred associated with body dysmorphia. This is a real-world mental health concept that is not visible in the image but is necessary to understand the meme's potential psychological impact.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_29d83ed0"
      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
    },
    {
      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_1c58d222",
      "@type": "BackgroundKnowledge",
      "instance_name": "self_esteem",
      "label": "Self-Esteem",
      "description": "The meme implicitly references the psychological concept of self-esteem, which refers to an individual's overall sense of personal worth or value. The text 'when you are that ugly you don't have a choice' suggests that appearance negatively impacts one's self-esteem, implying that those who are perceived as 'ugly' have less control over their self-worth. This is a real-world psychological concept that is not visible in the image but is necessary to understand the meme's message.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_29d83ed0"
      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
    },
    {
      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_bd7aaf03",
      "@type": "BackgroundKnowledge",
      "instance_name": "beauty_standards",
      "label": "Beauty Standards",
      "description": "The meme implicitly references the real-world concept of beauty standards, which are societal norms that define what is considered attractive or desirable in appearance. The text 'when you are that ugly you don't have a choice' contrasts with the idea that beauty standards are arbitrary and can be harmful, as they often lead to negative self-perception and discrimination against those who do not conform. Understanding this context is necessary to interpret the meme's critique or reinforcement of these standards.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_29d83ed0"
      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
    },
    {
